<title>UK: Dominican Republic joins ICCO.</title>
<headline>Dominican Republic joins ICCO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dominican Republic has become a member of the International Cocoa Agreement, the International Cocoa Organisation (ICCO) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>It officially became a member when its instrument of accession was received by the Secretary-General of the United Nations on 6 February.</p>
<p>The Dominican Republic accounts for 2.09 per cent of the world's exports for the purposes of the agreement, the ICCO said. This means that its exporting members now account for 91.33 per cent of total world exports of cocoa beans.</p>
<p>&quot;This is extremely good news which shows the continued confidence of producing countries in the work of the organisation,&quot; the ICCO said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
